SUMMARY:Ify Nwadiwe LIVE at The Bell House
DESCRIPTION:This post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nIfy Nwadiwe Live at The Bell House\nIfy NwadiweUm\, Actually on Dropout TV. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Saturday\, July 11\, 2026\nDoor Time: 6:30 PM | Show Time: 7:30 PM\nVenue: The Bell House\, 149 7th Street\, Brooklyn\, NY 11215\nAge Requirement: 21+ with valid government-issued photo ID\nSeating:\n\nAbout Ify Nwadiwe\nIfy Nwadiwe is a comedian\, actor\, writer\, and host based in Los Angeles. He’s appeared on Workaholics\, Comedy Bang! Bang!\, and Adam Ruins Everything. He writes for hit shows like Twisted Metal and Grand Crew\, and has contributed to major video games including Apex Legends and Borderlands 4. He’s best known to internet comedy fans as the host of Um\, Actually on Dropout TV. \nWhat to Expect\nA night of sharp\, nerdy\, and hilarious stand-up comedy from one of the most creative minds in comedy today. Ify’s unique perspective and rapid-fire wit make for an unforgettable live show. \nVenue Information\nThe Bell House149 7th Street\, Brooklyn\, NY 11215By Subway: Take the F\, G or R Train to the Smith-9th Streets station. \nTicket Information\nTickets start at approximately $35. There is an 8-ticket limit per order. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nDisclaimer: This post contains affiliate links. Purchasing tickets through our links helps support this site at no additional cost to you.
