SUMMARY:John Mulaney: Mister Whatever LIVE at Wrigley Field
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets\n \nAbout John Mulaney\nJohn Mulaney is one of the most celebrated stand-up comedians of his generation. The Emmy Award-winning writer and performer first rose to national prominence as a writer for Saturday Night Live\, before launching a stand-up career that has produced some of the most beloved comedy specials of the past decade — including New in Town\, The Comeback Kid\, Kid Gorgeous\, and Baby J. \nKnown for his razor-sharp storytelling\, his impeccable timing\, and his ability to turn deeply personal experiences into universally hilarious comedy\, Mulaney has built one of the most devoted fan bases in stand-up. His Mister Whatever tour has been selling out arenas and stadiums across North America\, and this Chicago date is the crown jewel of the entire run. \nOn July 11\, 2026\, John Mulaney will make history as the first comedian to ever headline Wrigley Field — one of the most iconic sports and entertainment venues in the world. This is a once-in-a-lifetime event for Chicago comedy fans. \nEvent Details\n\nEvent: John Mulaney: Mister Whatever\nDate: Saturday\, July 11\, 2026\nShow Time: 8:00 PM CT\nVenue: Wrigley Field\nAddress: 1060 W Addison St\, Chicago\, IL 60613\nNote: Tickets are non-transferable for this event\n\nAbout Wrigley Field\nWrigley Field is one of the most iconic and beloved sports venues in the United States. Built in 1914\, the home of the Chicago Cubs seats approximately 41\,000 fans and is renowned for its ivy-covered outfield walls\, its classic manual scoreboard\, and its unmatched atmosphere in the heart of Chicago’s Wrigleyville neighborhood. \nHosting a comedy show at Wrigley Field is an unprecedented event — the historic ballpark has never before hosted a stand-up comedian as a headliner. The venue is easily accessible via CTA Red Line (Addison station) and is surrounded by bars\, restaurants\, and the vibrant energy of Wrigleyville. Parking is available in the surrounding neighborhood\, though public transit is strongly recommended. \nWhat to Expect\nJohn Mulaney’s Mister Whatever is a full headline stand-up show featuring all-new material. Expect the signature Mulaney experience — brilliantly crafted storytelling\, perfectly timed punchlines\, and the kind of deeply personal comedy that feels both intimate and epic\, even in a stadium setting. \nThis is a historic night for Chicago comedy. Seeing John Mulaney perform stand-up at Wrigley Field is an experience that will be talked about for decades. Arrive early to soak in the atmosphere of one of baseball’s most storied venues transformed into a comedy stage. \nTicket Information\nTickets for John Mulaney: Mister Whatever at Wrigley Field start from $165. Purchase official tickets through Ticketmaster or find resale tickets through VividSeats. \n\nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets\n \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/john-mulaney-mister-whatever-live-at-wrigley-field/
LOCATION:Wrigley Field\, 1060 W Addison St\, Chicago\, IL\, 60613\, USA
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://media.ticketmaster.com/en-us/dam/a/b30/ccd9ebe2-c301-4487-bbe4-5bd6be744b30_TABLET_LANDSCAPE_LARGE_16_9.jpg
